//!
//! @page tool_usage Tool usage guide
//!
//! @brief User-facing map of the command-line tools and their normal flow.
//!
//! The usual entry point is `vcsc`. It accepts source, assembly, object,
//! and archive inputs, dispatches the lower-level tools, and writes the final
//! Intel HEX image unless stopped at an earlier stage.
//!
//! @section tool_usage_pipeline Normal pipeline
//!
//! - `vcsc-cc1` compiles `.c26` source into assembly.
//! - `vcsc-as` assembles source into relocatable `.o26` objects or Intel HEX.
//! - `vcsc-ar` bundles `.o26` objects into `.l26` archives for lazy linking.
//! - `vcsc-ld` links objects and archives, lays out memory, resolves relocations,
//!   emits Intel HEX, reports occupied/free cartridge ROM space, and optionally
//!   writes a map file containing the same usage summary.
//! - `vcsc-sim` can run an emitted HEX image for smoke and regression checks.
//!
//! @section tool_usage_examples Examples
//!
//! High-level flow:
//!
//! @code{.sh}
//! vcsc -I libraries/vcs examples/01_blank_screen/blank_screen.c26 -o solid_color.bin
//! @endcode
//!
//! Direct stage-by-stage flow:
//!
//! @code{.sh}
//! vcsc-cc1 -quiet -I libraries/vcs examples/01_blank_screen/blank_screen.c26 -o solid_color.s26 -dumpbase solid_color.c26 -dumpbase-ext .c26 -dumpdir ./
//! vcsc-as -I libraries/runtime/ -o solid_color.o26 solid_color.s26
//! vcsc-ld -T libraries/vcs/vcs_4k.cfg -o solid_color.bin solid_color.o26 libraries/runtime/libvcsc.l26
//! @endcode
//!
//! @section tool_usage_docs More detailed command references
//!
//! The top-level `README.md` summarizes installation, testing, and the
//! end-to-end workflow. The per-tool README files under `compiler/`,
//! `assembler/`, `linker/`, and `archiver/` describe each command in more
//! detail. Maintainers should start with the module pages linked from the
//! main page and then follow the documented internal functions in the source
//! browser.
